    "overview": {
      "summaryHtml": "",
      "detailsHtml": "<p><strong>Cetirizine hydrochloride (Allergy Relief)</strong> is an oral product that provides temporary symptomatic relief of hay fever and other upper respiratory allergic symptoms. It is intended to relieve—but not cure—typical allergic complaints affecting the nose and eyes.</p>\n\n<p>Key symptomatic targets:</p>\n<ul>\n  <li>Runny nose (rhinorrhea)</li>\n  <li>Sneezing</li>\n  <li>Itchy, watery eyes</li>\n  <li>Itching of the nose or throat</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>Use this product for patients who present with typical allergic rhinitis or similar upper respiratory allergy symptoms and need short-term symptomatic control. Follow the product’s labeled dosing instructions; if symptoms persist or worsen, advise clinical follow-up.</p>\n\n<div class=\"medlens-callout clinical\"><span class=\"medlens-callout-label\">Clinical note</span><p>This therapy provides temporary symptom relief—counsel patients that ongoing or worsening symptoms warrant medical evaluation rather than continued self-treatment.</p></div>",
      "title": "Overview",
      "visualPrompt": "Photograph of an over-the-counter oral tablet pack labeled 'Allergy Relief (cetirizine HCl)' alongside informational leaflets",
      "aiEdited": true
    },
