  "practicalInformation": "<p><strong>Key formulations</strong></p>\n<ul>\n  <li>Tablets: 200 mg oral tablets.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Storage & handling</strong></p>\n<ul>\n  <li>Store at controlled room temperature 20–25°C (68–77°F).</li>\n  <li>Protect from light and keep in a tight, light‑resistant container.</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"medlens-callout warning\"><span class=\"medlens-callout-label\">Clinical caution</span><p>There have been cases, some fatal, of overdose. Monitor cardiac rhythm and blood pressure. For significant bradycardia consider a β‑adrenergic agonist or temporary pacing. Treat hypotension with positive inotropic and vasopressor agents. Amiodarone and its metabolite are not dialyzable.</p></div>\n<div class=\"medlens-callout patient\"><span class=\"medlens-callout-label\">Patient counseling</span><p>Avoid grapefruit juice and St. John's Wort. Seek prompt medical attention for new or worsening shortness of breath or cough (possible pulmonary toxicity), fainting or pronounced slowing of heart rate, visual changes, or symptoms of hypo‑ or hyperthyroidism. Inform your prescriber if pregnant or planning pregnancy; breastfeeding is not recommended during treatment.</p></div>\n<div class=\"medlens-callout clinical\"><span class=\"medlens-callout-label\">Clinical note</span><p>Keep communication concise with patients about long half‑life and potential for delayed adverse effects; counsel on adherence and to report new systemic symptoms promptly.</p></div>"
