      "pediatric": {
        "summaryHtml": "<p>Safety and effectiveness of ceftriaxone for injection in neonates, infants and pediatric patients have been established for the dosages described in the DOSAGE AND ADMINISTRATION section.</p>",
        "detailsHtml": "<h4>Pediatric Use</h4><p>Pediatric Use Safety and effectiveness of ceftriaxone for injection in neonates, infants and pediatric patients have been established for the dosages described in the DOSAGE AND ADMINISTRATION section. In vitro studies have shown that ceftriaxone, like some other cephalosporins, can displace bilirubin from serum albumin. Ceftriaxone for injection should not be administered to hyperbilirubinemic neonates, especially prematures (see CONTRAINDICATIONS).</p>"
      }
