    "formulation": {
      "summaryHtml": "<p>Formoterol is available in several formulations internationally.</p>",
      "detailsHtml": "<p>Formoterol is available in several formulations internationally.</p><h4>Dry-Powder Inhalation</h4><p>Historically and in some markets:</p><p><strong>Formoterol fumarate 12 micrograms per inhalation/capsule</strong></p><p>The capsule is intended <strong>for inhalation through the specified device and must not be swallowed</strong>.</p><h4>Nebulized Inhalation Solution</h4><p>Common COPD formulation:</p><p><strong>20 micrograms/2 mL unit-dose vial</strong></p><p>Administered approximately every 12 hours.</p><p>Current U.S. nebulized formoterol products are indicated for COPD, not asthma. (<a href=\"https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/lookup.cfm?setid=c77e5f67-01bc-4704-8120-0e2e3d020482&amp;version=3&amp;utm_source=chatgpt.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">DailyMed</a>)</p><h4>Fixed-Dose ICS/Formoterol Combinations</h4><p>These are particularly important for asthma.</p><p>Examples include:</p><p><strong>Budesonide + formoterol</strong></p><p>and</p><p><strong>Beclometasone + formoterol</strong></p><p>GINA 2026 identifies budesonide-formoterol and beclometasone-formoterol among the combinations that can provide AIR therapy, and appropriate ICS-formoterol products can be used for MART. (<a href=\"https://ginasthma.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/GINA-2026-Strategy-Report-WMS.pdf?utm_source=chatgpt.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Global Initiative for Asthma - GINA</a>)</p><p>---</p>"
    },
